   "id": "fed-hike-talk-yields",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Fed hawks talk up more hikes as the 10-year yield holds above 5%",
   "when": "Tue 17 Nov · US session",
   "what": "St. Louis Fed president Alberto Musalem said several rate increases will likely be needed before spring 2027, possibly four. The funds rate range is 3.75%-4%. Traders priced a 95% chance of a quarter-point hike in December. The 10-year yield was about 5.11% and the 2-year about 4.81%. October core retail sales rose 0.6%, above the 0.4% expected. The S&P 500 closed at 7,340.53, down 1.03%, and the Nasdaq fell 0.74%.",
   "why": "Higher-for-longer rates weigh on large US stocks and their funds. Your two US funds, about 17% of the portfolio, are priced at 13 Nov. The S&P 500 is down 2.92% since then, so that fall is not yet in their NAVs. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive.",
