   "headline": "KOSPI slips under 5,000 as foreigners dump chip stocks",
   "when": "Tue 17 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI closed at 4,968.48, down 2.59%, its first close under 5,000 since 2 Feb. Foreign investors sold a net 1.45 trillion won. Samsung Electronics fell 3.30% to 190,300 won and SK hynix fell 1.96% to 1,098,000 won. The won weakened to 1,338.2 per dollar. Analysts pointed to doubts about Nvidia's leadership and new US rules aimed at stopping remote access to advanced AI chips.",
